(a) whether the Ministry, in coordination with national integration schemes, has organized student and youth exchange programmes between Chhattisgarh and the North Eastern States;
(b) if so, the details of participation levels and cross-cultural learning achieved under these initiatives;
(c) whether best practices in bamboo crafts and organic farming from the North East are being shared with Chhattisgarh's tribal artisans; and
(d) the details of subsequent livelihood benefits generated?

(a) whether the PM-KUSUM scheme has successfully achieved massive solarization of agricultural pumps across Chhattisgarh; 
(b) the details of off-grid solar pumps installed for tribal farmers in Financial Year 2025-26; 
(c) whether this historic green initiative has eliminated diesel dependency and provided reliable daytime irrigation; and
(d) the resulting boost to crop yields, farmer incomes, and the State's carbon footprint reduction?
GK

(a) whether transparent coal block auctions by the Centre have significantly boosted revenue sharing for the State of Chhattisgarh;
(b) if so, the record revenue generated and transferred during the last three years;
(c) whether Government successfully utilized District Mineral Foundation (DMF) funds for inclusive growth in tribal and coal-bearing regions; and
(d) if so, the details of land compensation, rehabilitation, healthcare, education, and drinking water projects measures taken?

(a) the total financial benefits transferred directly to farmers in Chhattisgarh under the Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi (PM-KISAN) Scheme over the last three years;
(b) the number of beneficiaries actively receiving installments under the Scheme in the State;
(c) whether the Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) has successfully provided timely claim settlements to farmers affected by erratic weather; and
(d) the details of claims settled and the overall financial security provided to the State's agriculture sector?

(a) the steps taken to accelerate the adoption of electric vehicles in Chhattisgarh under the FAME and PM E-Drive schemes;
(b) the total number of electric vehicles incentivized and EV charging stations successfully operationalized across major cities and highways in the State;
(c) whether financial support has been extended to modernize heavy engineering or manufacturing units in Chhattisgarh; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and its contribution to green mobility?

(a) the steps taken to revive and promote traditional handloom and silk weaving clusters, such as Kosa silk, in Chhattisgarh;
(b) the details of financial assistance, modern toolkits, and design upgradation training provided to tribal weavers under the National Handloom Development Programme (NHDP);
(c) whether e-commerce onboarding initiatives have successfully given local artisans direct access to national and global markets; and
(d) the overall increase in household income among the State's weaver communities?

(a) the initiatives taken by the Archaeological Survey of India (ASI) to preserve and restore historical temple complexes like Sirpur and Bhoramdeo in Chhattisgarh;
(b) the total financial assistance allocated for these heritage conservation projects over the last three years;
(c) whether Government has launched specific programs to document and promote the unique tribal art, folklore and cultural traditions of Bastar; and
(d) the progress made in establishing digital cultural repositories?
J

(a) the progress of BharatNet project in connecting all Gram Panchayats of Chhattisgarh with high-speed optical fiber;
(b) the number of rural panchayats actively utilizing digital services under this initiative;
(c) the steps taken to rapidly expand 4G and 5G mobile connectivity in Left Wing Extremism (LWE) affected districts; and
(d) how many new mobile towers have been installed to bridge the digital divide for tribal populations?

(a) whether the multi-pronged strategy against Left Wing Extremism (LWE) has dramatically reduced security incidents and expanded development in Chhattisgarh;
(b) the details of security infrastructure funds and Special Central Assistance allocated to the State's most affected districts; and
(c) whether the surrender and rehabilitation policies have successfully brought misguided youth into the mainstream?

(a) whether the Central Government has successfully expanded the 'Krishi Udan 2.0' scheme in the State of Chhattisgarh to facilitate swift agricultural exports;
(b) the details of the airports integrated and the volume of tribal forest produce and agri-products transported;
(c) whether the deployment of kisan drones is being heavily incentivized for local farmers; and
(d) the resulting milestones in enhancing the shelf-life of perishable goods and drastically improving farmers' incomes?

(a) the steps taken to boost manufacturing and non-traditional exports from Chhattisgarh under the One District One Product (ODOP) initiative;
(b) the infrastructure and logistics support provided to local industries to access global markets;
(c) whether the Startup India initiative has successfully nurtured tech and agri-startups across the State; and
(d) the details of registered startups and financial incentives provided to encourage young entrepreneurs in Chhattisgarh?

(a) the initiatives taken to promote grassroots innovation and scientific research among student communities in Chhattisgarh through the INSPIRE scheme;
(b) the total research grants and fellowships awarded to institutions in the State during the last three years;
(c) whether dedicated biotechnology clusters or rural technology parks have been established to add value to local minor forest produce; and
(d) the resulting boost to rural entrepreneurship?

(a) the number of unorganized workers from Chhattisgarh registered on the e-Shram portal;
(b) the details of social security benefits and accidental insurance cover extended to such workers;
(c) whether the PM Shram Yogi Maan-dhan (PM-SYM) pension scheme has seen robust adoption among informal workers in the State; and
(d) the steps taken to strictly enforce welfare standards and wage security across local industrial sectors?

(a) the progress of the computerization of Primary Agricultural Credit Societies (PACS) in Chhattisgarh to bring absolute transparency to rural credit;
(b) the details of funds released and PACS successfully integrated into the national software;
(c) whether the establishment of Multi-State Cooperative Societies for seeds and organic products has expanded livelihood opportunities for local farmers; and
(d) the details of the World's Largest Grain Storage Plan (WLGSP) being implemented within the State's cooperative sector?

(a) whether Government has successfully expanded aviation infrastructure in the State of Chhattisgarh under the UDAN scheme;
(b) if so, the details of new routes and passenger growth at Bilaspur, Jagdalpur, and Ambikapur airports during the last three years;
(c) whether funds were allocated for terminal upgradation and modern facilities to meet rising demand; and
(d) if so, the details thereof and the positive impact on local tourism and economic growth?

(a) whether schemes like Pradhan Mantri Janjatiya Unnat Gram Abhiyan (PM-JUGA) are being extended to tribal minority areas in Raigarh, Chhattisgarh;
(b) if so, the details of funding and activities under Dharti Aaba Janjatiya Gram Utkarsh Abhiyan (DAJGUA);
(c) if not, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the steps for tribal minority welfare and skill development in the region?

(a) whether Government supports expansion of National Minorities Development and Finance Corporation (NMDFC) schemes in the State of Chhattisgarh;
?(b) if so, the details of the proposed measures;
(c) if not, the reasons therefor; and
(d) the steps being taken to enhance minority entrepreneurship through NMDFC?

(a) whether it is a fact that AIIMS Raipur has a specific number of beds, ICU beds, and specialties currently operational;
(b) if so, the details of the total number of beds, ICU beds, and specialties available at AIIMS Raipur;
(c) the details of vacant positions for nursing staff and doctors at AIIMS Raipur, and the steps being taken to address these vacancies; and
(d) the future plans for expansion and improvement of infrastructure, medical facilities, and services at AIIMS Raipur?

(a) whether Government has any plan to utilize mining areas in the State of Chhattisgarh, after the exhaustion of coal reserves, for promoting tourism and recreational activities;
(b) if so, the details of proposed initiatives such as eco-parks, sites for water sports, underground tours, golf grounds and avenues for recreation, adventure or bird watching;
(c) the steps being taken to transform such areas in the State of Chhattisgarh into sustainable tourism hubs; and
(d) whether any consultations with stakeholders or pilot projects have been undertaken in the State in this regard?

(a) whether Government plans to introduce international flight operations at Swami Vivekananda airport, Raipur;
(b) if so, the details of the proposed measures;
(c) if not, the reasons for not implementing such measures; and
(d) the steps being considered to enhance connectivity through Swami Vivekananda airport in Raipur?

(a) whether Government is aware that many CGHS beneficiaries aged above 75 years living alone in remote or rural areas need to travel long distances, often 200–300 kilometres, to access treatment at CGHS-empanelled hospitals; 
(b) if so, whether any assessment has been conducted on the difficulties faced by such elderly beneficiaries; 
(c) whether Government proposes to allow them treatment at nearby non-empanelled hospitals on a cashless basis; and 
(d) if so, the details of mechanisms for authorisation, reimbursement, and other steps to ensure accessible healthcare?
